    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0012:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0012",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "In the example below, the [`removeDuplicates(by:)`](publisher/removeduplicates(by:).md) functionality triggers when the `x` property of the current and previous elements are equal, otherwise the operator publishes the current `Point` to the downstream subscriber:",
      "normalizedSource": "In the example below, the [`removeDuplicates(by:)`](publisher/removeduplicates(by:).md) functionality triggers when the `x` property of the current and previous elements are equal, otherwise the operator publishes the current `Point` to the downstream subscriber:",
      "sourceHash": "b9aa2536c429397f24b0ea46f29c4bd7ade3fdad50cbc52e18c559af1328945b",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Use the [`removeDuplicates(by:)`](publisher/removeduplicates(by:).md) operator when comparing types that don’t themselves implement `Equatable`, or if you need to compare values differently than the type’s `Equatable` implementation.",
      "contextAfter": "```swift\nstruct Point {\n    let x: Int\n    let y: Int\n}\n\nlet points = [Point(x: 0, y: 0), Point(x: 0, y: 1),\n              Point(x: 1, y: 1), Point(x: 2, y: 1)]\ncancellable = points.publisher\n    .removeDuplicates { prev, current in\n        // Considers points to be duplicate if the x coordinate\n        // is equal, and ignores the y coordinate\n        prev.x == current.x\n    }\n    .sink { print(\"\\($0)\", terminator: \" \") }\n\n// Prints: Point(x: 0, y: 0) Point(x: 1, y: 1) Point(x: 2, y: 1)\n```",
      "documentTitle": "removeDuplicates(by:)",
      "framework": "Combine",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
